Follow-up to karr #38 (Langertha::Engine::Hetzner).

Hetzner's OpenAI-compatible endpoint advertises tools on the wire shape,
but the Hetzner Inference API docs do NOT explicitly confirm server-side
tool support. The engine currently ships with tools_native=true (per
OpenAI-compatible wire) + a POD caveat noting this uncertainty.

Goal:
1. Run t/88_live_hetzner.t with TEST_LANGERTHA_HETZNER_API_KEY +
   TEST_LANGERTHA_HETZNER_TEST_TOOLS=1 against each of the four catalog
   models (Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8, DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731,
   GLM-5.2-NVFP4, Kimi-K2.7-Code).
2. Record pass/fail per model in the ticket.
3. For each model that 400s on tools, add an
   'around engine_capabilities' override clearing tools_native /
   tool_choice_* and recording the model-specific tool-list to the
   pre-existing capability notes (mirrors what engines like Perplexity
   do today).
4. If at least one model succeeds, keep tools_native=true and add a
   clearer POD note ('tool support verified on Qwen+Qwen3.6, not yet
   on DeepSeek/GLM/Kimi' or similar).
5. If none succeed, demote tools_native=false and move to a Hermes-style
   XML fallback (new role composition) — escalate before that.

No merge until at least the live run lands; per karr #36 verification
runbook format. Live tests cost real money — gate the run behind
TEST_LANGERTHA_HETZNER_API_KEY and pick one model per chat window.

